#: ../../source/babylon_README.md:26
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babylon_README.md:28
msgid "`babylon.parse(code, [options])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babylon_README.md:30
msgid "`babylon.parseExpression(code, [options])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babylon_README.md:32
msgid ""
"`parse()` parses the provided `code` as an entire ECMAScript program, "
"while `parseExpression()` tries to parse a single Expression with "
"performance in mind. When in doubt, use `.parse()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babylon_README.md:36
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babylon_README.md:38
msgid ""
"**allowImportExportEverywhere**: By default, `import` and `export` "
"declarations can only appear at a program's top level. Setting this "
"option to `true` allows them anywhere where a statement is allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babylon_README.md:42
msgid ""
"**allowReturnOutsideFunction**: By default, a return statement at the top"
" level raises an error. Set this to `true` to accept such code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babylon_README.md:46
msgid "**allowSuperOutsideMethod**: TODO"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babylon_README.md:48
msgid ""
"**sourceType**: Indicate the mode the code should be parsed in. Can be "
"either `\"script\"` or `\"module\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babylon_README.md:51
msgid ""
"**sourceFilename**: Correlate output AST nodes with their source "
"filename.  Useful when generating code and source maps from the ASTs of "
"multiple input files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babylon_README.md:53
msgid ""
"**startLine**: By default, the first line of code parsed is treated as "
"line 1. You can provide a line number to alternatively start with. Useful"
" for integration with other source tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babylon_README.md:55
msgid "**plugins**: Array containing the plugins that you want to enable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/babylon_README.md:57
msgid "**strictMode**: TODO"
msgstr ""

